  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "TRIAL EDITION - SQL longer than 10,000 characters is rejected (parse() returns -1). Full edition: https://www.sqlparser.com\n\nRelease 4.1.0.18\n\n- [MSSQL] Complete lineage for the 41 SQL Server inputs that 4.1.0.17\n  listed as deferred; they no longer report SyntaxError.\n- [MSSQL] Accept CREATE COLUMN MASTER KEY, COLUMN ENCRYPTION KEY,\n  DATABASE ENCRYPTION KEY, EVENT SESSION, EXTERNAL LANGUAGE and\n  EVENT NOTIFICATION, security policy predicates and extended GRANT.\n- [MSSQL] Accept FORCE DISTRIBUTED PLAN and FOR TIMESTAMP AS OF hints,\n  ALTER COLUMN ADD/DROP HIDDEN, PERSISTED and NOT FOR REPLICATION,\n  index REBUILD and columnstore ORDER variants, and --1 in expressions.\n- [MSSQL] Split view bodies and DDL continuations into statements the\n  same way with and without lineage analysis.\n- [MSSQL] Release lineage request metadata from a pooled worker after\n  a spill IO failure. Fix Boolean and repeated-element XML decoding.\n- [PostgreSQL] Parse PREPARE into TPrepareStmt (Mantis 4868).\n- [PostgreSQL] Support INSERT ... ON CONFLICT, TABLE t queries, a CTE\n  body that starts with WITH, and keyword-qualified type names.\n\nDemos: https://github.com/sqlparser/gsp_demo_dotnet",
